	"notes": "Waabi is a self-driving-truck company's homepage, and — like the other creative agency-style site in this batch (mocean-home) — every screenshot we took shows the same thing: a full-screen video of a truck with a headline on top. That is a deliberate design choice (a big, cinematic opening), not a broken capture, and the page's own code proves there is much more beneath it: a stats section, a technology section, a partnerships section, and a row of seven case-study cards that looks built to scroll sideways. We simply cannot show any of that in a picture, because those sections are sized to fill whatever the screen's height is, and a taller \"whole page\" screenshot just makes the first section taller instead of revealing the next one. We also found zero stylesheets in the network traffic for this page, so unlike every other site in this batch we cannot even guess a pixel breakpoint from the CSS — the responsive story here rests entirely on the DOM shapes, not on any confirmed number.",
